# Flutter Architecture

## Directory Structure

Use feature-based directory structure:
```
lib/
  feature_name/
    data/           # Repositories, data sources, models
    domain/         # Business logic, entities, use cases
    presentation/   # UI widgets, pages, state
```

## Patterns

- Separate UI from business logic — no business logic in widgets
- Use repository pattern for data access
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use const constructors wherever possible
- Proper widget lifecycle management (dispose streams, controllers, listeners)
- Navigator 2.0 / go_router for navigation

## Widget Design

- Keep build methods focused — extract sub-widgets when build exceeds 40 lines
- Prefer StatelessWidget when no mutable state is needed
- Use keys properly for widget identity in lists
- Avoid GlobalKey unless absolutely necessary

## Dependency Injection

- Register dependencies in dedicated files, not inline
- Use lazy singletons for expensive services
- Use factories for per-use instances
- Reset DI container in test setUp
